You are making a final styling and layout change to the Park Finder take-home in /Users/tom/park-finder (Angular 22, zoneless, signals, Vitest). Work on main, uncommitted. Do NOT run any git command except `git diff` and `git status`. No new dependencies. Nothing outside the file list. If something is unclear or surprises you, stop and report instead of guessing.

Read first: /Users/tom/park-finder/CLAUDE.md (binding conventions), then src/app/parks-page.{ts,html,css,spec.ts}, src/app/panel/park-panel.{ts,html,css,spec.ts}, src/app/app.{html,css}. Everything is on main and committed; the tests are green (9 files, 90 tests).

Every shell command must start with: export NVM_DIR="$HOME/.nvm"; . "$NVM_DIR/nvm.sh"; nvm use 24.21.0 >/dev/null;  and use `npx ng`, never bare `ng`.

Files you may touch: src/app/app.css, src/app/parks-page.{html,css,spec.ts}, src/app/panel/park-panel.{html,css,ts,spec.ts}. Not parks-page.ts (its signals, `recenter()`, `toggleSheet()`, `onMapFocusIn()`, `expanded`, `fitRequest` stay as they are).

Tom's three requests:
1. The blue bar buttons (Back `.back`, sheet toggle `.sheet-toggle`) look odd next to the Recenter button. All three bar controls get the Recenter style: white icon, transparent background, 1px solid white border (`color: var(--color-surface); background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--color-surface)`), same 44×44 minimum and radius. Add a subtle hover: `background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface) 15%, transparent)`. Drop the separate `.recenter` override since the shared rule now covers it.
2. The bar needs a little padding underneath: the bar padding becomes `var(--space-2) var(--space-3)` on all sides (today it has 0 at the bottom).
3. The panel heading ("Parks" in list mode, the park name in details mode, "Park not found" for an unknown id) moves into the brown bar, centered between the left control and the right slot, white text. "Park Finder" is centered in the green header (`h1 { text-align: center }` in app.css).

How to do request 3 (decided, do it this way): the bar moves from the page template into ParkPanel, and the page projects its controls into it. This keeps the h2 and the focus logic inside ParkPanel so the existing focus specs stay valid.

- park-panel.html becomes:
  ```
  <div class="panel-bar">
    <div class="slot"><ng-content select="[data-slot='start']" /></div>
    <h2 id="panel-heading" tabindex="-1" #heading>{{ title() }}</h2>
    <div class="slot"><ng-content select="[data-slot='end']" /></div>
  </div>
  <div class="panel-body">
    @if (selectedId() === undefined) {
      <nav aria-labelledby="panel-heading">
        …the existing loading / error / empty / <ul class="park-list"> content, unchanged, but WITHOUT the old <h2 id="parks-heading" #listHeading>…
      </nav>
    } @else if (loading()) {
      <p role="status">Loading parks…</p>
    } @else if (error()) {
      <p role="alert">{{ error() }}</p>
    } @else {
      @if (selected(); as park) {
        <article>
          …the existing details content, unchanged, but WITHOUT the <h2 tabindex="-1" #detailsHeading> (the heading is now in the bar)…
        </article>
      } @else {
        <p>No park matches this link.</p>
      }
    }
  </div>
  ```
- park-panel.ts: add `protected readonly title = computed(() => { const id = this.selectedId(); if (id === undefined) return 'Parks'; const park = this.selected(); if (park) return park.name; return this.loading() || this.error() !== null ? 'Parks' : 'Park not found'; })`. Replace the two heading refs `listHeading` / `detailsHeading` with one `heading = viewChild.required<ElementRef<HTMLHeadingElement>>('heading')`. Update the `afterRenderEffect` accordingly: in details mode (id defined) focus `heading` once per id exactly as before (`id !== this.lastFocusedId`); in the return-to-list branch the fallback target is `heading` instead of `listHeading`. Keep the "does not steal focus" guard and its comment. Keep `lastFocusedId` and `lastOpenedId` as plain fields. Nothing else in the class changes.
- park-panel.css: `:host { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; min-height: 0; }`. `.panel-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px 1fr 44px; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); background: var(--color-secondary); }` (fixed 44px side columns keep the title centered even when the end slot is empty on desktop). `.slot { display: flex; }` and `.slot:last-child { justify-content: flex-end; }`. `.panel-bar h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-surface); font-size: 1.1rem; text-align: center; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }` (it may wrap to two lines for long names; never shrink below 16px). `.panel-bar :focus-visible { outline-color: var(--color-surface); }` with the existing contrast comment moved here from parks-page.css. `.panel-body { flex: 1; min-height: 0; padding: var(--space-3); overflow-y: auto; }` (it is now the one scroll container; padding inside it keeps focus rings from being clipped). Remove the old `h2 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); color: var(--color-primary); }` rule (no h2 remains in the body). Keep everything else.
- parks-page.html becomes:
  ```
  <main #sheet [class.is-expanded]="expanded()">
    <div id="sheet" class="sheet-content">
      <app-park-panel [parks]="parks()" [loading]="loading()" [error]="error()" [selectedId]="id()">
        @if (id() !== undefined) {
          <a data-slot="start" class="back" routerLink="/parks" aria-label="Back to parks" title="Back to parks">…existing svg…</a>
        } @else {
          <button data-slot="start" type="button" class="recenter" …existing…>…existing svg…</button>
        }
        @if (isMobile()) {
          <button data-slot="end" type="button" class="sheet-toggle" …existing attributes…>…existing svg…</button>
        }
      </app-park-panel>
    </div>
  </main>
  <aside …unchanged…>
  ```
  Note: projected content inside `@if` blocks is fine in Angular 22; `ng-content select` matches by the `data-slot` attribute. Check that `ng-content` with a select on an attribute inside a control-flow block projects correctly (it does, because the `@if` is inside the parent's template; if the build or a test says otherwise, stop and report).
- parks-page.css: `.sheet-content { flex: 1; min-height: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }` (no padding, no overflow; the panel body scrolls now). Remove `.panel-bar` and `.panel-bar :focus-visible` rules from here (moved to the panel). Keep the shared `.back, .recenter, .sheet-toggle` rule here (projected nodes keep the page's style scope) and change it per request 1; remove the `.recenter` override. Keep the `.sheet-toggle svg` rotation rules and `main.is-expanded .sheet-toggle svg` (the `main.is-expanded` ancestor still exists). Keep both media blocks and the keep-in-sync comments.
- app.css: `h1 { text-align: center; }` added to the existing rule.

Specs (update first, then implement; run `npx ng test --watch=false` for a failing run excerpt, then again for green):
- park-panel.spec.ts: the h2 is now inside `.panel-bar`, still inside the component, so `h2(fixture)` keeps working. Update: the not-found case asserts `text(h2)` is "Park not found" and that the body text contains "No park matches this link."; `links every park by name` keeps `nav ul a`; add a case: list mode h2 text is "Parks" and `nav` has `aria-labelledby="panel-heading"`; add a case: while loading with an id the h2 says "Parks" (not "Park not found"); the "does not steal focus" case still focuses `article h3` (fine). Every focus case stays as is and must still pass (open → activeElement is the h2 with the park name; back → the link; switching → new heading text; deep link; deep link finishing loading; first list render does not move focus).
- parks-page.spec.ts: `heading()` reads the first h2, now in the bar; existing cases should pass unchanged. Add: in details mode the bar order is Back, then h2, then (mobile only) the toggle, checked with `compareDocumentPosition` via the existing `precedes()` helper; on desktop `main .panel-bar h2` text is "Parks" on /parks and "Prospect Park" on /parks/prospect-park. The existing selectors `main .panel-bar` and `main button[aria-controls="sheet"]` still match because the bar is inside main.

Then `npx prettier --write .`, `npx ng build` (no warnings), `npx ng test --watch=false` (all green). Report: `git diff --stat`, the full `git diff`, the failing-run excerpt, the passing test summary and build summary, and anything you deviated from or were unsure about.

Conventions: signals, computed, built-in control flow, OnPush, no `any`, plain CSS with tokens, scoped component styles, native elements, no global classes, no new dependencies. Minimum text size 16px everywhere.

